<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The abaddon folk's pawn kind. She is the one kind in this mod that NO faction
		lists: neither tribe names her in pawnGroupMakers and neither lists her in its
		xenotypeSet, so a village never raises her and a raid never brings her.

		The kind exists for two reasons, both about being able to reach her at all:

		* The dev-mode spawn list is a list of pawn kinds, so without one she cannot
		  be spawned for testing at all - she existed only as a xenotype, reachable by
		  dev "apply xenotype", which is a way of converting a pawn rather than making
		  a new one. A kind is generated, so she arrives as a whole species: her race,
		  her four-armed body and her xenotype in one step.
		  (Converting a pawn works too: core's XenotypeRacePatch applies a xenotype's
		  declared race whenever a living pawn is given one. Big & Small itself only
		  reads it while a pawn is generated, so before that patch the converted pawn
		  wore her genes on its old body - no four arms, no wings, no chitin.)
		* Anything that wants her by name - a quest, another mod, a patch, a future
		  spawn source - needs a def to name.

		combatPower 35 puts her between the greenworm (25) and the devil bug (40): a
		soldier bug is quick and hard-shelled, but she is half a human's size. The
		number only matters if she is ever put in a pawn group, which today she is not.
	-->
	<PawnKindDef ParentName="PMM_InsectKindBase">
		<defName>PMM_InsectAbaddonFolk</defName>
		<label>abaddon folk</label>
		<race>PMM_Race_AbaddonFolk</race>
		<combatPower>35</combatPower>
		<backstoryFilters>
			<li>
				<categories>
					<li>PMM_AbaddonFolkSpawn</li>
				</categories>
			</li>
		</backstoryFilters>
		<xenotypeSet><xenotypeChances><PMM_InsectAbaddonFolk>100</PMM_InsectAbaddonFolk></xenotypeChances></xenotypeSet>
	</PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
